From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:29:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc/intel/cannonlake: Turn on the DMI Power Optimizer by
 default

PchPwrOptEnable, the DMI Power Optimizer of the PCH, is off by default
in the Coffee Lake FSP-S (CoffeeLakeFspBinPkg: 0 in the UPD region of
fsps.bin), and Cannon Lake never set it. Tiger Lake and Alder Lake
turn it on unless a board sets DmiPwrOptimizeDisable.

On an M920x (Q370) whose PCIe links all have ASPM L1 and LTR, whose
PMC sees no LTR under 150 us and whose iGPU sits in RC6 without a
display, the package never goes past PC3 (89-94% of the time at idle,
never PC6 to PC10).

Do as the later SoCs: on unless the devicetree sets
DmiPwrOptimizeDisable.

TEST=Built lenovo/m920x. Package C-states of the M920x after it, in
the hardware test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/soc/intel/cannonlake/chip.h       | 6 ++++++
 src/soc/intel/cannonlake/fsp_params.c | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/chip.h b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/chip.h
index b8fd376a50..27be8f1abd 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/chip.h
+++ b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/chip.h
@@ -395,6 +395,12 @@ struct soc_intel_cannonlake_config {
 	/* SATA Power Optimizer */
 	bool satapwroptimize;
 
+	/*
+	 * DMI Power Optimizer of the PCH, on unless a board sets this, as
+	 * on Tiger Lake and Alder Lake: FSP-S has it off by default here
+	 */
+	bool DmiPwrOptimizeDisable;
+
 	/* SATA Gen3 Strength */
 	struct sata_port_config sata_port[SOC_INTEL_CML_SATA_DEV_MAX];
 
diff --git a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/fsp_params.c b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/fsp_params.c
index bd2e808c33..bbf69a2bd8 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/fsp_params.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/fsp_params.c
@@ -440,6 +440,9 @@ void platform_fsp_silicon_init_params_cb(FSPS_UPD *supd)
 	s_cfg->PchPmPcieWakeFromDeepSx = config->LanWakeFromDeepSx;
 	s_cfg->PchPmWolEnableOverride = get_uint_option("wake_on_lan", config->WolEnableOverride);
 
+	/* DMI Power Optimizer: lets the PCH report its idleness to the CPU */
+	s_cfg->PchPwrOptEnable = !config->DmiPwrOptimizeDisable;
+
 	/* disable Legacy PME */
 	memset(s_cfg->PcieRpPmSci, 0, sizeof(s_cfg->PcieRpPmSci));
 
